elf wrote it and in writing it I  couldn't redo that at 37 now it's it's  I'm just a different person at this  point but it did capture the best of me  in fact I've had four false starts  writing trying to write a book a  follow-up book to this but they haven't  worked because it's like man I said  everything I need to say in this one  book and it's hard to sort of keep it  going in fact we have a question about  that little bit later but Ryan I'll let  you get to your pithy answers because  we're almost out of time here  cool pit the answer is perfection is  impossible adding value is priceless so  Zac what I'm trying to tell you is is  yes put something out there man like do  the best job that you can with the  constraints that you have in fact if you  don't have any constraints try to put a  constraint on there to kind of force  yourself to put something out there but  except that it's never gonna be perfect  and also know like as you continue to  put stuff out five years from now you're  gonna be so much better if you wait five  years and don't put anything out you're  not gonna feel nearly as good all right  next question is from chocolate mmm  chocolate how do you defeat shyness and  self-doubt well I don't have to put the  answer for this one but I could tell you  the one thing that I did because I'm an  extreme introvert like I spent 80 90  percent of my time alone I I value that  alone time but I was also very socially  incompetent like in high school and the  thing that I did was I got a job that  make made me work with people every  single day and it's it's you know when  you teach a baby to swim you can just  literally throw them in the water I know  you can't it just sounds funny  no babies in the water but if you if you  don't do it if you wait till they're 2  or 3 then they drown but if you do with  it with an infant you can sit my mom did  this with me and just I I think she was  trying to get rid of me but she just  chucked me in the water and you s